{
    "file": "Leading_and_Managing_Breakthrough_Innovation.docx",
    "title": "Leading and Managing Breakthrough Innovation",
    "duration": "3 Days",
    "overview": [
        "Breakthrough innovation requires leaders to move beyond incremental improvement and create the conditions in which genuinely new value can emerge. This involves identifying significant opportunities, challenging established assumptions, mobilizing diverse thinking, managing uncertainty, testing ideas intelligently, and protecting promising innovations from being eliminated too early by conventional operating logic.",
        "This course equips leaders and managers with a practical framework for leading breakthrough innovation from opportunity identification through experimentation and implementation. Participants will examine innovation strategy, disruptive opportunities, customer and stakeholder insight, creative problem framing, idea generation, portfolio thinking, experimentation, risk, governance, cross-functional collaboration, leadership behavior, and the transition from promising concept to scalable organizational value.",
        "The program combines strategic thinking with practical innovation management. Through cases, opportunity-framing exercises, ideation workshops, concept evaluation, experimentation design, portfolio decisions, and implementation planning, participants will develop an actionable approach for leading innovation while balancing ambition, evidence, resources, and organizational realities."
    ],
    "audience": [
        "Senior managers, department heads, business-unit leaders, innovation managers, strategy professionals, transformation leaders, project and program managers, product and service development leaders, operations managers, public-sector leaders, and professionals responsible for identifying, sponsoring, developing, or implementing significant innovation initiatives."
    ],
    "methodology": [
        "The course uses an interactive methodology combining short presentations, innovation case studies, strategic opportunity analysis, assumption-challenging exercises, problem-framing workshops, structured ideation, concept development, portfolio exercises, experimentation design, risk analysis, stakeholder mapping, implementation planning, group discussion, and action planning. Participants will apply the tools to realistic organizational challenges and develop practical breakthrough-innovation initiatives."
    ],
    "competencies": [
        "Innovation leadership",
        "Strategic opportunity identification",
        "Creative problem framing",
        "Breakthrough thinking",
        "Idea generation and evaluation",
        "Experimentation and learning",
        "Innovation portfolio management",
        "Risk and uncertainty management",
        "Cross-functional collaboration",
        "Stakeholder engagement",
        "Innovation governance",
        "Innovation implementation"
    ],
    "objectivesIntro": [
        "By the end of the course, participants will be able to:"
    ],
    "objectives": [
        "Differentiate incremental, adjacent, disruptive, and breakthrough innovation.",
        "Identify strategic opportunities for breakthrough innovation using customer, market, technology, and organizational insight.",
        "Challenge assumptions and reframe problems to create new innovation possibilities.",
        "Lead structured idea generation and convert promising ideas into clear innovation concepts.",
        "Evaluate innovation opportunities without applying inappropriate conventional criteria too early.",
        "Design experiments that test critical assumptions and generate useful evidence.",
        "Manage uncertainty, risk, resources, and learning across an innovation portfolio.",
        "Create leadership conditions that support psychological safety, experimentation, and constructive challenge.",
        "Build cross-functional support and stakeholder commitment for innovation initiatives.",
        "Develop practical pathways for moving successful concepts toward implementation and scale.",
        "Create an action plan for strengthening breakthrough innovation within the organization."
    ],
